# FRU Chassis Info Area (FRU spec section 10). Parsed by
# fru_area_print_chassis() in lib/ipmi_fru.c. The area size must be a multiple
# of 8 bytes and the last byte is the zero checksum over the whole area.
#
# The length and checksum bytes are reserved in place and filled in at the end,
# because the checksum covers the length byte.

@mark area
01           # [0] Format version 1
@mark lenslot
00           # [1] Area length / 8 (filled in below)
17           # [2] Chassis type 17h = Rack Mount Chassis
c5 43 48 2d 30 31                # Part number,   8-bit ASCII, 5 chars: "CH-01"
c6 53 4e 43 48 30 31             # Serial number, 8-bit ASCII, 6 chars: "SNCH01"
c1                               # C1h: no more fields in this area
@pad 6 0x00                      # Pad to a multiple of 8 bytes
@mark sumslot
00                               # [23] Zero checksum (filled in below)
@fill_size8 lenslot area
@fill_checksum sumslot area
